\details{
Each work is looked up by the first identifier of \code{by} that it has: its
OpenAlex id (\code{works$openalex_id}, shortened to the \code{W} number) or its
DOI (normalised on both sides, so \verb{https://doi.org/} prefixes and case
do not matter). Works without either are counted and left as they are.
A DOI that contains \verb{,} or \code{|} cannot be written into an OpenAlex
filter; such works are left out and counted too. The identifiers are
sent in batches of \code{batch_size} (at most 100, the number of values an
OpenAlex filter takes), with only the fields needed (\code{select}). When
OpenAlex has several records for one DOI, the record with the most
yearly citations is used, then the one with the lowest OpenAlex id.

The fields are joined with \code{\link[=sm_materialise]{sm_materialise()}} (\code{overwrite = TRUE}). All
five values of a work found come from its OpenAlex record, \code{NA} where
the record has none, so a new run replaces the values of an earlier run
or of another source, and the values, their date (\code{citations_as_of})
and the yearly counts of a work always belong to one record. The works
not found keep their values. Only these five \code{works} columns change;
\code{cited_by_count} and the other columns keep the values of their source.
The \code{citations_by_year} rows of every work found are replaced by the
counts OpenAlex has now; the rows of the other works stay.
\code{metadata$last_refresh} is not changed.

Every work found gets a provenance row with the source
\code{"openalex_impact"}, its OpenAlex id in \code{source_id_external}, a short
description of the call in \code{query} and the kind \code{"enrichment"}, so
\code{\link[=sm_rebuild_from_cert]{sm_rebuild_from_cert()}} never replays the step as a search. Neither
the API key nor any request URL or filter is stored.

On HTTP 429 (the request budget is used up) the function stops at once
and joins nothing, not even the batches fetched before: a partial
enrichment would compare works with OpenAlex values against works
without them. The error
(class \code{scimapR_openalex_rate_limit}) names the reset time, the
remaining budget OpenAlex reports and the key setting. Any other failed
request stops it too (class \code{scimapR_openalex_failed}).
